# Working-tree line endings are LF, always.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` was set on this machine, which means Git checked files out with
# CRLF while the repository stores LF. That is invisible in a diff and it broke a
# build gate: `gofmt -l` reported two files as unformatted, because gofmt rewrites
# CRLF to LF and so considers a CRLF file "not formatted".
#
# It also silently disabled four mutation anchors. They are Go string literals
# containing "\n", so a multi-line anchor can never match a CRLF file -- every
# single-line anchor still matched, every multi-line one did not, and the checker
# reported "patch did not apply" for a file that was demonstrably clean.
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` makes the working tree agree with the repository and with gofmt,
# so neither the gate nor the harness can be broken again by a checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# These must never be treated as text to be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary